  "notes" : [
    "Keys are the RFC 8032 section 7.1 TEST 1 and TEST 2 Ed25519 keys: published test constants that must never sign anything real.",
    "Ed25519 is deterministic, so every signature below is reproducible from the key and the preimage.",
    "Account objects are fixed-layout byte strings, not gua-lp.v1: they have no optional fields, sets or free strings, and the accountId is a permanent hash so the hashed bytes must be the bytes that crossed the wire.",
    "An accountId has exactly one spelling. 34 bytes are 272 bits and 55 base32 characters carry 275, so the final character holds three unused bits and is always one of a, i, q, y.",
    "A conforming implementation reproduces every canonicalHex, sha256Hex, accountId and signature, and refuses every entry under rejections with the reason named there."
